      "answer": "Perform hand hygiene at five moments: before touching a patient, before a clean or aseptic procedure, after body fluid exposure risk, after touching a patient, and after touching patient surroundings. During an outbreak of Clostridioides difficile, use soap and water for all care of affected patients and increase environmental cleaning. Encourage patients and visitors to clean their hands and to ask staff whether they have done so.",
