      "answer": "For soap and water, wet the hands, lather for at least 40 seconds, rinse and dry with a single-use towel. Use soap and water when hands are visibly dirty, and after caring for a patient with Clostridioides difficile or norovirus, because alcohol is less effective against spores and non-enveloped viruses. Wash with soap and water for 40 to 60 seconds when hands are visibly soiled or contaminated with blood or body fluids.",
